 "response": "Toris's budget is now **$1,677K**.\n\n**Method**\n- Only Finance Office budget messages count. Messages from Marketing, PMO, Vendor calls and other teams were ignored. So were Finance Office notes that don't change the budget, such as room moves and receipts.\n- Each withdrawal chain was resolved from the end. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so the update it targeted stands again.\n- Examples:\n  - #0002 (\u2212$561K) stands. #0417 withdraws #0170, which reinstates #0035, which withdraws #0003. So #0003 no longer cancels #0002.\n  - #0010 (\u2212$303K) is withdrawn. #0505 withdraws #0088, which reinstates #0070, which withdraws #0025. That leaves #0016 in force, cancelling #0010.\n  - #0014 (\u2212$501K) is withdrawn. #0958 cancels #0339, so #0258 stands. #0258 cancels #0054, so #0047 stands and withdraws #0014.\n  - Updates #0007, #0006, #0020, #0078, #0350 and #0063 were resolved the same way. The first five stand. #0063 is withdrawn by #0373.\n- About 110 budget updates end up withdrawn. Examples are #0004, #0015, #0046, #0098, #0139, #0236, #0447, #0642, #0879, #1131 and #1178.\n\n**Calculation**\nThe budget starts at $1,710K (#0001). Every update still in force was then applied in record order.\n\nCheckpoints in the running total:\n- after #0100: $2,036K\n- after #0400: $2,436K\n- after #0800: $1,841K\n- after #1200: $1,192K\n- after #1600: $1,677K\n\nANSWER: $1677K",
